<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAfrica money mkt shortage rises to 9.65 bln rand.</title>
<headline>SAfrica money mkt shortage rises to 9.65 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The money market shortage rose to 9.65 billion rand on Thursday from 9.378 billion rand on Wednesday, latest Reserve Bank figures show. </p>
<p>Banks quoted their three-month NCD rates unchanged at between 16.95 percent and 17.00 percent offered, while the 90-day BA rate was also unmoved at between 16.30 and 16.60 percent.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
